# Implementation Plan - TinyML Neural Network Deployment on ESP32 Waist Belt

This implementation plan details deploying a **TinyML (TensorFlow Lite / Quantized Neural Network)** inference engine directly onto the **ESP32 Waist Belt Firmware**. This enables real-time AI fall detection (`NORMAL`, `SUDDEN_MOVEMENT`, `PREFALL`, `FALL`) running directly on the ESP32 hardware in **< 20 milliseconds**, functioning seamlessly in both **Offline and Online Mode**.

---

## Technical Architecture

```
[PyTorch Model (ml-service)]
         │
         ▼
[Export & Quantize: export_tinyml.py]
         │
         ▼
[tinyml_model.h (C++ Byte Array)] ──► Embedded in ESP32 Sketch
         │
         ▼
[ESP32 TinyML Engine (waist_belt_workaround.ino)]
         │
         ├──► On-Device Inference (< 20ms execution)
         ├──► OFFLINE: Local Speaker "Help! Help!" + GSM SIM800L SMS + 1-Min Mic Recording
         └──► ONLINE: Local Speaker + Mic + Twilio SMS + Spring Backend & Mitra AI Sync
```

